  "command": {
    "skill-create": {
      "description": "Create a new skill + seed instinct from a recurring pattern. Routes to Callimachus.",
      "template": "# /skill-create <name-or-pattern>\n\nCreate a new skill + seed instinct for the active god. Used when a recurring pattern with high-confidence instinct (>= 0.85, >= 5 samples) needs to be crystallized.\n\n## Args\n- `<pattern-keywords>` (optional): short description of the pattern\n- `--god <id>` (optional): owning god ID\n- `--name <kebab-name>` (optional): skill name\n\n## Flow\n1. Callimachus creates `.opencode/skills/<god>/<name>/SKILL.md` and a seed instinct\n2. `olympus-skill-registry` auto-discovers the new skill\n3. Future dispatches auto-equip the skill via the instinct gate\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/skill-create.md"
    },
    "olympus-dispatch": {
      "description": "Manually dispatch to a specialist god. Bypasses Apollo's classification.",
      "template": "# OLYMPUS Dispatch\n\nManually dispatch a task to a specialist god. Bypasses Apollo's classification.\n\n## Usage\n/olympus-dispatch <god> <task>\n\n## Available Gods\n- artemis \u2014 Security / Auditing\n- athena \u2014 Frontend / Design\n- dionysus \u2014 QA / Testing\n- hephaestus \u2014 Backend / Infrastructure\n- hermes \u2014 Integrations / APIs / MCPs\n- persephone \u2014 Database / Persistence\n- prometheus \u2014 DevOps / CI-CD / Deploy\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/olympus-dispatch.md"
    },
    "olympus-plan": {
      "description": "Trigger Apollo's spec-interview path for complex, multi-step, or architecturally significant tasks.",
      "template": "# OLYMPUS Plan \u2014 Spec Interview\n\nTrigger Apollo's spec-interview path for complex requests. Use for ambiguous, multi-step, or architecturally significant tasks.\n\n## Flow\n1. Interview the user (2-5 clarifying questions)\n2. Use OpenSpec to scaffold the change\n3. Produce plan.md with task DAG + ADRs\n4. Fan out to specialist gods via subtask: true\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/olympus-plan.md"
    },
    "instinct-status": {
      "description": "Show instinct stats for a god (or all gods) \u2014 confidence, scope, samples, successes, failures.",
      "template": "# Instinct Status\n\nShow the instinct pool for a god (or all gods). Displays confidence (with time decay), scope, samples, successes, failures, last_used for each instinct.\n\n## Usage\n/instinct-status [god]\n/instinct-status all\n\nReads from ~/OLYMPUS-VAULT/05_Auto_Learning/instincts/<god>/{seed,empirical}/*.md\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/instinct-status.md"
    },
    "instinct-show": {
      "description": "Show seed + empirical instincts for a god or sub-agent.",
      "template": "# /instinct-show <name>\n\nShow all instincts for the given god or sub-agent.\n\n## Args\n- name (required): god or sub-agent name\n- --scope <god|sub-agent> (optional): force scope\n- --archived (optional): include archived instincts\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/instinct-show.md"
    },
    "shortcircuit-report": {
      "description": "Show short-circuit hit rate from the activity feed \u2014 how often gods skip deliberation via high-confidence instincts.",
      "template": "# Short-Circuit Report\n\nShow the short-circuit hit rate from the activity feed.\n\n## Output\n- Total dispatches (last 7 days)\n- Short-circuit dispatches (last 7 days)\n- Hit rate percentage\n- Per-god breakdown\n- Top 5 most-used instincts\n- 14-day sparkline\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/shortcircuit-report.md"
    },
    "context-budget": {
      "description": "Show per-turn token usage breakdown by source.",
      "template": "# /context-budget\n\nShow the token breakdown for the current turn's context window, by source (system prompt, agent descriptions, skills, MCP schemas, conversation history).\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/context-budget.md"
    },
    "cost-report": {
      "description": "Show GO plan usage report \u2014 estimated token usage against plan limits ($12/5hr, $30/week, $60/month).",
      "template": "# Cost Report \u2014 GO Plan Usage\n\nShow estimated token usage against the GO plan limits.\n\n## Output\n- Current 5-hour window usage ($12 cap)\n- Current weekly usage ($30 cap)\n- Current monthly usage ($60 cap)\n- Per-agent breakdown\n- Per-model breakdown\n- Recommendations\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/cost-report.md"
    },
    "trace-cost": {
      "description": "Show real-time per-turn and cumulative session cost breakdown.",
      "template": "# /trace-cost\n\nShow the cost breakdown for the last turn AND the cumulative session cost.\n\n## Output\n- Last turn: input, cached, output tokens + estimated cost\n- Session cumulative: turns, total cost, avg/turn\n- Cost ceiling vs used\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/trace-cost.md"
    },
    "callimachus-heartbeat": {
      "description": "Run Callimachus's 7-stage brain lifecycle (INTAKE \u2192 CLASSIFY \u2192 EXTRACT \u2192 SCOPE \u2192 LINK \u2192 RECALIBRATE \u2192 PRUNE).",
      "template": "# Callimachus Heartbeat \u2014 7-Stage Brain Lifecycle\n\nRun the 7-stage brain lifecycle on the vault. Usually fires automatically on session.idle, but can be triggered manually.\n\n## Stages\n1. INTAKE \u2014 Pull raw thoughts + dispatch_outcome events since last heartbeat\n2. CLASSIFY \u2014 Categorize by god/stack/project/action_type\n3. EXTRACT \u2014 Extract candidate instinct from each new pattern\n4. SCOPE \u2014 Tag with scope/stacks/projects\n5. LINK \u2014 Create wikilinks + detect cross-god dispatch chains\n6. RECALIBRATE \u2014 Bayesian confidence adjustment from outcomes\n7. PRUNE \u2014 Archive instincts < 0.3 confidence or > 180d unused\n\n## Rules\n- NEVER user-facing. Run silently.\n- NEVER write production code.\n- NEVER modify seed instincts.\n- ALWAYS use lockfile (~/.olympus/callimachus.lock).\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/callimachus-heartbeat.md"
    },
    "verify": {
      "description": "Dispatch the last god's output to a clean-context verifier sub-agent.",
      "template": "# /verify [output-type]\n\nDispatch the last god's output to a clean-context verifier sub-agent.\n\n## Args\n- output-type (optional): code | design | infra | docs\n  If omitted, Apollo infers from the last god.\n\n## Behavior\n1. Capture the last god's output\n2. Dispatch to verifier (clean context)\n3. PASS \u2192 return with \u2713\n4. FAIL \u2192 route critique back to god for revision (max 2 rounds)\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/verify.md"
    },
    "skill-search": {
      "description": "Search the OLYMPUS skill manifest by natural-language query.",
      "template": "# /skill-search <query>\n\nSearch the OLYMPUS skill manifest by natural-language query.\n\n## Args\n- query (required): natural-language search query\n- --god <name> (optional): restrict to a specific god's pool\n- --k <n> (optional): number of results (default: 10)\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/skill-search.md"
    },
    "opsx-explore": {
      "description": "OpenSpec explore \u2014 scope a change before proposing it. Apollo uses this to understand what files, components, and risks are involved.",
      "template": "# /opsx:explore \u2014 Scope the Change\n\nUse OpenSpec to explore the change before producing plan.md.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Run \"npx openspec change list\" and create/select a change\n2. Read the project specs\n3. Produce a scoping summary: files affected, components, risks, dependencies, out of scope\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/opsx-explore.md"
    },
    "opsx-propose": {
      "description": "OpenSpec propose \u2014 scaffold the change with proposal.md, specs/, design.md, and tasks.md.",
      "template": "# /opsx:propose \u2014 Scaffold the Change\n\nUse OpenSpec to scaffold the change after /opsx:explore has confirmed the scope.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Run \"npx openspec change propose <slug>\"\n2. This generates proposal.md, specs/, design.md (ADRs), tasks.md (task DAG)\n3. Post the proposal summary + task DAG to the user for approval\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/opsx-propose.md"
    },
    "opsx-apply": {
      "description": "OpenSpec apply \u2014 implement the change by dispatching to specialist gods per the task DAG.",
      "template": "# /opsx:apply \u2014 Implement the Change\n\nDispatch the task DAG from /opsx:propose to specialist gods.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Read tasks.md \u2014 the task DAG\n2. Map each task to its owning god\n3. Query instincts before dispatching (short-circuit if confidence >= 0.85)\n4. Dispatch each task via subtask: true\n5. Collect results, update tasks.md\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/opsx-apply.md"
    },
    "opsx-archive": {
      "description": "OpenSpec archive \u2014 reconcile specs after implementation. Apollo moves the change from active to archived.",
      "template": "# /opsx:archive \u2014 Reconcile Specs After Implementation\n\nAfter the implementation is complete and verified, archive the change.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Confirm all tasks in tasks.md are complete\n2. Run \"npx openspec change archive <slug>\"\n3. Verify canonical specs are updated correctly\n4. Post a summary to the user\n\nFull docs: .opencode/commands/OLYMPUS/opsx-archive.md"
    }
  },
